# Patches are applied with `git apply`, which matches context lines
# byte-for-byte against the LF sources extracted from the QuickJS tarball.
# A CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the default on Windows and on
# GitHub Actions runners) makes every context line mismatch and the patch
# fails to apply. Keep patch files byte-for-byte identical everywhere.
*.patch -text

# The official CSS 2.1 snapshot is hash-pinned in test-suites.lock.json and verified by
# scripts/fetch-tests.ps1 on every CI run. Any end-of-line rewrite on commit or checkout
# (core.autocrlf=true is the Git default on Windows) would change the bytes and break the
# pin, so keep the vendored tree byte-exact everywhere.
Lite.Conformance/vendor/css21-official-20110323/** -text
